From eb37432633b7714410ccd02f9b29dc3cd53f5bee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cass <867000+Cass67@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:41:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] spec: implement Laguna S 2.1 DFlash support

Ported from the minimal patch in ggml-org/llama.cpp#26669 (Joe Rowell /
sdroege) onto our build tree (b10909 + unsloth PRs 144/137 + 0008). Two
rebases were needed:

  - #27310 fused the DFlash encoder into the KV cache injection path after
    that patch was written, so Laguna aux RMS-norm has to be replicated
    there or the injected K/V come from a different space than the encoder.
  - PR 144 adds an MTP impl whose member block is textually identical to
    the DFlash one, so the n_layer_tgt declaration lands in the wrong
    struct under git am fuzz. Anchored to the dflash struct explicitly.

Adds the gated-attention drafter variant: enc.aux_norm and the per-layer
attn_gate weights, which is the 76-vs-69 tensor gap that makes every
published Laguna DFlash gguf fail to load on stock master.
